    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our offensive core is headlined by **Lawrence Butler** (73.47) and **Daulton Varsho** (68.37), both of whom benefit from favorable matchups against pitchers with xERAs above 4.50. **Lawrence Butler** is our standout play, buoyed by a significant +16% boost from the opposing starter's skill profile and a +13% platoon edge. Similarly, **Daulton Varsho** thrives in his matchup against Rea, where his combination of power and SB potential against a pitcher with mediocre hold rates makes him a high-floor start. Meanwhile, **Bryson Stott** (63.12) is a fascinating play; while his overall score is slightly lower, he remains a critical component of our strategy due to the 92% SB efficiency factor against the opposing battery, making him an essential asset in our push to close the gap in the scarcest category.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was leaving **Drew Gilbert** (39.49) out of the starting nine. He fell just shy of our 40-point threshold, hampered primarily by an unfavorable 8th-place lineup projection that stifled his scoring potential compared to the high-upside roles held by **Jonathan Aranda** (56.90) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (59.39). While **Jonathan Aranda** faces a tougher park environment, his elite xwOBA of 0.377 and favorable platoon split kept him safely in the mix. We continue to monitor the status of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith**, both of whom remain sidelined on the IL, leaving us to rely on the depth of players like **Taylor Ward**, who, despite a tough draw against Yamamoto, draws into the lineup with a wind-out advantage that provides a marginal boost to his power profile. \n\nRisks for this rotation are centered on the volatility of \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Cal Raleigh**, **Yainer Diaz**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Tyler Freeman**, **Lawrence Butler**, and **Taylor Ward**. If any of these hitters are shuffled to the bottom of their respective batting orders, their scores will regress accordingly. Furthermore, while we are cautious with **Taylor Ward** against an elite arm like Yamamoto, the weather-driven wind advantage forces our hand to prioritize his plate appearances. We are effectively balanced between high-ceiling platoon plays and steady contributors like **Luis Arraez** and **Matt Chapman**, who provide the necessary floor to protect our game caps while we hunt for SBs from **Bryson Stott** and **Daulton Varsho**.",
